@startuml ledger-trial-lifecycle
' ============================================================================
' Failure-atomic bounded private ledger trial (task 7921): the control flow of
' run_trial in IncrementalLedgerTrial.v and of TrialCase::run_from in the Rust
' test model rspace++/tests/persistence/incremental_reachability_properties.rs.
'   GREY   #616161  the predecessor: read, never written
'   BLUE   #1565C0  a phase start: its charge is reserved before any step
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  accepted cursor steps and the prepared evidence
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  budget guards
'   RED    #C62828  refusals: each one returns the predecessor unchanged
'   PURPLE #6A1B9A  the partial-commit negative control
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam StateBorderColor #455A64
skinparam StateFontSize 13
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64

title <b>A bounded private ledger trial</b>\nevery transition is charged before it is accepted, and every refusal keeps the predecessor

state "Predecessor" as Base #E0E0E0 : <latex>\pi = (\Lambda, R, O, B)</latex>\nledger, root multiplicities,\nobject and byte inventory
state "Authorize removals" as Authorize #FFE0B2 : <latex>\mathrm{occ}_\rho(v) \le R(v) + \mathrm{occ}_\alpha(v)</latex>\nfor every removed vertex
state "Activation start" as ActivationStart #BBDEFB : events = added occurrences, no frames\nreserve <latex>|\alpha|</latex> live scratch and <latex>|\alpha|</latex> references
state "Activation steps" as Activation #C8E6C9 : the scheduled cursor step:\nevent (increment), transfer, or discard
state "Deactivation start" as DeactivationStart #BBDEFB : events = removed occurrences, no frames\nreserve <latex>|\rho|</latex> live scratch and <latex>|\rho|</latex> references
state "Deactivation steps" as Deactivation #C8E6C9 : the scheduled cursor step:\nevent (decrement), transfer, or discard
state "Final guard" as Final #FFE0B2 : final objects, then final bytes
state "Prepared evidence" as Prepared #A5D6A7 : ledger, roots, objects, bytes, usage\nno durable receipt, no owner authority
state "Refused(why)" as Refused #FFCDD2 : retained predecessor = <latex>\pi</latex>, bit for bit
state "PartialCommit mutant" as Partial #E1BEE7 : retained = the in-flight ledger

[*] --> Base
Base --> Authorize
Authorize -[#C62828]-> Refused : UnauthorizedRemoval
Authorize -[#1565C0]-> ActivationStart : authorized
ActivationStart -[#C62828]-> Refused : Budget(first exceeded step axis)
ActivationStart -[#2E7D32]-> Activation : within limits
Activation -[#2E7D32]-> Activation : charge, guard, accept
Activation -[#C62828]-> Refused : Budget(axis) or PotentialExhausted
Activation -[#1565C0]-> DeactivationStart : drained
DeactivationStart -[#C62828]-> Refused : Budget(first exceeded step axis)
DeactivationStart -[#2E7D32]-> Deactivation : within limits
Deactivation -[#2E7D32]-> Deactivation : charge, guard, accept
Deactivation -[#C62828]-> Refused : Budget(axis), ZeroCountDecrement,\nInventoryUnderflow or PotentialExhausted
Deactivation -[#EF6C00]-> Final : drained
Final -[#C62828]-> Refused : Budget(FinalObjects or FinalBytes)
Final -[#2E7D32]-> Prepared : within limits
Refused -[#6A1B9A,dashed]-> Partial : negative control only
Prepared --> [*]
Refused --> [*]

note right of Activation #F1F8E9
  One step from usage <latex>u</latex> with charge <latex>k</latex>:
  <latex>u' = \mathrm{commit}(u, k)</latex>
  refuse at the first step axis <latex>a</latex> with <latex>u'_a > L_a</latex>,
  in the order Count, UnionObjects, UnionBytes,
  Scratch, References, Expansions, QuotedBytes.
  A refusal leaves the whole trial state unchanged.
end note

note left of Refused #FFEBEE
  Retry from the retained predecessor with limits
  that cover the unbounded evidence <latex>e</latex>
  (<latex>\forall a.\ e_a \le L_a</latex>) prepares exactly <latex>e</latex>.
end note
@enduml
